course: dictionary
lesson: 2077
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them are the context, and they tell you which meaning is right. «A constitution is the set of basic rules for how a country is run» is about rules and government, so here constitution means the basic laws of a country.
explain: The second meaning is about the body. «A strong constitution» means someone who does not get ill easily. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: a strong set of laws does not make sense for a person, so this is the body meaning.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. If a sentence mentions a country, a government or rights, think laws. If it mentions health, illness or strength, think body.
fact: A constitution is the set of basic laws and rules that says how a country or group is governed.
fact: A person's constitution is how healthy and strong their body is.
fact: A club or school council can also have a constitution, which is its basic set of rules.
fact: The United States Constitution was written in 1787, and the first ten changes to it are called the Bill of Rights.
fact: The UK has no single written constitution, so its basic rules are spread across many laws and traditions.
exercise: «A constitution is the set of basic rules for how a country is run.» What does constitution mean here? | A person's healthy body | A football kit for a club | A new president's oath | *The basic laws and rules that say how a country is governed
exercise: «He has a strong constitution, so he hardly ever gets ill.» What does constitution mean here? | A loud shout at a football match | *How healthy and strong a person's body is | A very long set of laws | A rule about how to play a game
exercise: «The United States Constitution was written in 1787.» In which year was it written? | *1787 | 1709 | 20 January | 1775
test: «The Ukrainian constitution describes the flag as two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below.» In this sentence, what is a constitution? | *The basic laws and rules of a country | A club's rules for its members | A person who is healthy | A flag with three colours
test: Sam says, «My cousin has a strong constitution.» What does Sam mean? | *His cousin is healthy and rarely ill | His cousin lives in a country with no laws | His cousin is loud and bossy | His cousin writes the laws for his town
exam: Mia reads, «Many countries also wrote rights into their own laws, such as the US Bill of Rights.» Which meaning of constitution fits the words around it, and why? | A football kit, because kits have rules | *The basic laws of a country, because rights and laws are about how a country is governed | A club's list of games, because clubs have rights | A person's healthy body, because rights are about people's bodies
